# wlink directive — 3com-pktdrv (minimal floor milestone)
#
# Resident-first class ordering is what makes copy-down work: RESIDENT classes are placed
# first (lowest); after the composer emits the hot image we TSR-keep up to the end of the
# resident region, reclaiming everything above (composer/fragments/cold init).

system dos
name build/3cpd.exe
option quiet
option map=build/3cpd.map
option stack=2048

# Class ordering: the default DOSSEG-style order already places the hot code class (CODE:
# _TEXT) before the cold class (COLD_TEXT), which is what copy-down relies on. Verified in
# build/3cpd.map:  _TEXT @ 0000  ->  COLD_TEXT @ 0075 (after).  An explicit ORDER directive
# placing RESIDENT_DATA + EMIT_ARENA between them will be added when copy-down is implemented
# (it must pack resident data adjacent to resident code so the keep-boundary is tight).

# minimal floor object set
file build/api.obj
file build/packet.obj
file build/hal.obj
file build/compose.obj
file build/frag_pio.obj
file build/main.obj
file build/el3_core.obj
file build/el3_isa.obj
file build/cpu_detect.obj
file build/nic_irq.obj
